-- **8-cube ($gs$):** A set of 8 voxels $v_0 \dots v_7$ ordered by binary coding of the index. Voxels $v_i$ and $v_j$ are 26-connected if $i \neq j$ [S1].
-- **4-face:** One of the six inner faces of an 8-cube, composed of 4 voxels. Each 4-face is shared by exactly two 8-cubes. Inner 4-faces are oriented and ordered (e.g., clockwise) [S1].
